  "note": "Complete ancient MaribDam remains in the1843Arnaudsurvey phase: both northern and southern sluice assemblies and their stone retaining moles, three north/two south rounded gate abutments, exposed sluice channels, remnant masonry/earthfill bank arms with the great central breach left open, intrinsic northern curved revetment and separate ancient distribution basin. Primary pace/unit dimensions and drawing topology are approximate; hidden heights/sections and individual ruin profiles estimated. Exclude modern1986dam/upstreamreservoir, natural Balaqmountains/wadi/rockcliffs, distant city/temples/inscriptions as lettering and archaeological elements outside this dam system. This is a ruined historical structure, not a hypothetical restored intact ancient dam. Independent2048m129x129originalfield/16641heights/two rawTerrariumzoom14tiles/frame/datum1125.8859m acquired before north/south/basin floors and main masonry/earthbank sections. Original16mgrid and9.2115moutputpixels are not native survey accuracy or1843grade. Component floors fixed from original point samples+.5m; earthbank controls follow original independent field once, before geometry. Never flatten/reacquire/reframe/move floors or main sections for rendering. Representedyear1843; July31isdisplayconvention, not exact documented surveyday."
